ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2c13baccbdb34d4319034302c8a803e2a92a210904e4cf835ac4467c292689e4","event_uuid":"00860405-5b99-4caf-94cf-5a65961330c9","position":{"commit_sha":"71ece5dc5fb678dd411855b7bd00ce3618778e21","position":"1787721666864736001-00860405-5b99-4caf-94cf-5a65961330c9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787028379237708001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dabbdae7-ca53-43c1-848b-352878581d53","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1cb3-d60c-0d32-4cfe"},{"link_uuid":"c588498a-4151-4cc5-b405-b4bdc808653b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"12b1-5f66-2bff-4f10"},{"link_uuid":"8330c91b-0740-449c-b4a5-f717bb93d07d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"300c-ddc9-6bcc-4b9c"}],"description":"## Context\nThe create sequence must survive process restart without duplicate Jira issues, preserve index-lag grace, and release dependent links/children only after create and binding confirmation are proven. This task makes the coordinated create family AUTHORITATIVE on the LIVE outbound dispatch path behind ONE rollback selector.\n\n## Outcome\nRun the complete Cloud/DC crash-restart sequence twice, prove exactly one remote issue and one confirmed binding, then cut the LIVE outbound create over to the coordinated family behind one internal rollback selector, with legacy retained as the rollback value (its removal is S5).\n\n## Live consumers the cutover updates in lockstep (no-dual-send)\nThe single selector is `create_route.create_route()` (env `REBAR_RECONCILER_CREATE_ROUTE`; default COORDINATOR_ROUTE, one falsey LEGACY_ROUTE rollback value), mirroring `reconcile_helpers._write_facade_enabled`. Three live consumers are updated together so a create is dispatched by EXACTLY ONE route, never both:\n1. `batch_dispatch.route_for(\"create\")` → returns `create_route()` (create is governed by the selector, not left on a rejected/legacy default).\n2. `batch_dispatch.reroute_migrated_plans` — its predicate is pinned to `NON_CREATE_FAMILIES`, so a create-bearing plan is NEVER rerouted onto the S3 `coordinate_and_fuse` non-create surface; every live create stays on the single outbound-create dispatch.\n3. The LIVE outbound-create dispatch `applier._apply_batch → _apply_one → apply_handlers.handle_create → dispatch_one.create_one`: `handle_create` reads `create_route()` and selects the create→contain MIDDLE core once — coordinated (default) or legacy — and passes it into `create_one`. `create_one` keeps its shared prelude (budget/index-lag grace/dedup/field-translation) and postlude (user labels/comments); only the middle core differs. Mirrors the proven ADR-0103 `summary_executor` cutover in `handle_update`.\n\nNo-dual-send guarantee: `applier.apply()` selects typed vs batch dispatch by argument type per call (mutually exclusive); reroute excludes create; and the live batch create runs `create_one` exactly once whose middle core is EITHER coordinated OR legacy. Exactly one physical `create_issue` per create mutation under the coordinator route. The typed outbound-create leaf delegates to the SAME coordinated facade, so typed and batch share one implementation (no parity drift).\n\n## Plan\n1. Compose pending, create, containment, confirmation, and RP-02 keyed/keyless recovery across fresh process/store instances (`create_route.coordinate_full_create` over `coordinate_create` + `contain_created`).\n2. Preserve keyed recovery with zero search and keyless recovery with both three misses and 3600 seconds; one recovery failure cannot stop unrelated tickets.\n3. Hold create-before-link and parent-before-child dependents until proven create/confirmation (`should_hold_dependent` / `dependents_released`); preserve tombstones, filters, and read-only modes. Live create-before-link ordering is additionally enforced upstream by binding-confirmation-gated key resolution (a link cannot resolve its parent's Jira key until `bind_confirm`).\n4. Venue-gate Cloud/DC verified-fake crash/restart tests, then cut the LIVE outbound create over to the coordinated middle core via `handle_create`'s selector, retaining the legacy core behind the rollback value. Never run legacy and coordinator creates together.\n5. Preserve exact per-ticket tally, logs, known-key safety abort, and rollback by re-observation. The coordinated core adapts its outcome to `create_one`'s exact contract: return the create dict on confirmed; re-raise the ORIGINAL exception (preserving HTTPError taxonomy for the 404 soft-fail / non-404 fail-fast split) on permanent/persist/containment failure; emit the same no-delete BRIDGE_ALERT on a landed-but-unconfirmed create; and defer (append `deferred_creates`, return None) on commit-unknown without a second create.\n\n## Testing\nDuplicate probes execute every fault cut twice with fresh state through the LIVE batch entry point `applier.apply([...], pass_id=..., client, binding_store)`. Dependency and filter tables assert zero early effects and independent continuation. Contract-parity tests assert success/soft-404/fail-fast/landed-unconfirmed/persist-failure/commit-unknown all behave identically to legacy on the live path; shared prelude/postlude (dedup, budget, index-lag, events, comments) verified under both routes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every Cloud/DC crash-restart fault cut converges to exactly one remote issue and one confirmed forward/reverse binding.\n- [x] Keyed recovery performs zero search.\n- [x] Keyless negative search requires both three misses and 3600 seconds.\n- [x] Per-entry recovery failure does not stop unrelated tickets.\n- [x] Links and children wait for proven create/confirmation, while tombstones, filters, and read-only modes remain effective.\n- [x] Create has one coordinator route and one internal legacy rollback value with no dual-send, and the coordinator route is the LIVE outbound-create default (governing `route_for`, `reroute_migrated_plans`, and the `handle_create`/`create_one` dispatch in lockstep).\n\n## Out of scope\nFinal removal of legacy create helpers remains S5. End-to-end validation against live Jira Cloud + DC (no-duplicate-after-timeout, commit-unknown recovery, disabled SDK retry) is gated by the epic's required Live External Integration workflow.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/create_route.py","reason":"New create route selector + pure coordinate_full_create composition (create+containment) + dependent gate + live outbound wiring; the cutover core."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_outbound.py","reason":"Cut the outbound create leaf to the coordinated write-ahead path by default; legacy create+delete-rollback retained only behind the rollback selector."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound.py","reason":"Consult the single selector for symmetry; confirmation gates dependents while retired/dedup short-circuits are preserved."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py","reason":"route_for decides create via the single selector; reroute predicate pinned to non-create families so a create is never mis-routed to coordinate_and_fuse."},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Document the REBAR_RECONCILER_CREATE_ROUTE rollback selector."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_create_operation_coordinator.py","reason":"Cloud/DC crash-restart oracle, dependency gating, route/no-dual-send, known-key safety abort."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_write_ahead_recovery.py","reason":"Keyed zero-search regression + write-ahead order through the coordinated path."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py","reason":"Keyless unbind requires both 3 misses and 3600s; index-lag duplicate prevention."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_filter.py","reason":"Per-entry recovery failure independence; filter/read-only/tombstone zero-early-effect under the coordinator route."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_leaves_effect_matrix.py","reason":"Outbound create leaf now exercised on both routes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_coordinator.py","reason":"route_for create-selector regression."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_apply_outbound_create_rollback.py","reason":"Legacy create+delete-rollback pinned behind the rollback selector."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"Extracted create_one's create->contain MIDDLE core into _legacy_create_core (the rollback value) behind a zero-branch create_core selector kwarg (complexity 36->27); prelude/postlude unchanged. The live batch create seam the coordinated core slots into."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"handle_create reads create_route() and selects the create MIDDLE core once (_select_create_core) — the SINGLE live-batch consumption point for the selector, mirroring the ADR-0103 summary_executor cutover. Binds deferred_creates+mutation for commit_unknown defer."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_create_live_cutover_heldout.py","reason":"Held-out live-path tests driving the real applier.apply([create_dict],...) batch entry point across both routes; assert one create + forward/reverse binding + outcome/REST count + 404 soft-fail + non-404 fail-fast + landed-unconfirmed no-delete alert (contract parity)."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","1cb3-d60c-0d32-4cfe"],["parent","59b0-d1b9-ad94-4339"],["relates_to","12b1-5f66-2bff-4f10"],["relates_to","300c-ddc9-6bcc-4b9c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"59b0-d1b9-ad94-4339","parent_status_uuid":"b980122c-39a0-4379-9187-b1548cb4c1d0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp03","create","recovery","tdd"],"ticket_id":"2863-c335-4567-4430","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S4 T3 — Prove restart convergence and cut over create coordination","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_create_operation_coordinator.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_filter.py","dd_id":"AC1,AC4-AC6","dd_text":"Crash/restart uniqueness, independent recovery, dependency/filter behavior, and create cutover"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_write_ahead_recovery.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py","dd_id":"AC2-AC3","dd_text":"Keyed/keyless recovery and index-lag grace"}]},"source_event_uuids":["187cd07d-8558-4f25-a946-db9a2fb02072","152d05d0-7791-4248-a0e5-2164b4a7606c","76196499-0afb-4082-b681-9d480b6590f9","b1b9808a-5dd3-4e74-8818-f901a70db02d","939dc01a-a1f4-4082-ab8f-b8cce9abd140","25488691-baa8-4d0e-9cf1-ec1efb9fb72f","c588498a-4151-4cc5-b405-b4bdc808653b","b3390a8a-b98c-483b-9869-d87cb645a3bb","a81d8ce9-2170-4c74-bfd6-39906ae6ce3f","6ba48f19-6815-46ab-b2d0-8e8a86f0fe5d","8330c91b-0740-449c-b4a5-f717bb93d07d","b980122c-39a0-4379-9187-b1548cb4c1d0","00860405-5b99-4caf-94cf-5a65961330c9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787727155971324001,"uuid":"24cf68af-5cca-4ea2-928d-67804d8fb05b"}